<title>USA: Rotary Power cuts 34 pct of workforce.</title>
<headline>Rotary Power cuts 34 pct of workforce.</headline>
<dateline>WOOD-RIDGE, N.J. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rotary Power International Inc (RPI) said Thursday it had terminated 20 of its employees, or 34 percent of its workforce, in an effort to reduce costs as its military contract business ends.</p>
<p>The end of the military contracts comes earlier than RPI expected when it began operations in 1992 and before commercial engine activities have reached a point where they are profitable.</p>
<p>During the first three quarters of 1996, RPI said it has experienced negative cash flow of about $270,000 per month.</p>
<p>If such rate of negative cash flow continues, RPI said its current and anticipated cash resources are expected to be sufficient to fund its operations for two more months.</p>
</text>
